{
 "text": "This entire video was made from a text file. No editor, no camera, no timeline.\n\nSave this if you've ever wanted to post every day without filming anything.\n\nHere's the entire stack. Claude Code writes the script as a simple list of beats: what the voice says, and what shows on screen.\n\nElevenLabs reads it out loud and returns the exact timestamp of every single word.\n\nThat's why each word pops the moment it's spoken.\n\nThen Remotion, a free tool that turns React code into video, animates everything: the text, the icons, the camera moves.\n\nEven the music underneath was generated from a one-line prompt.\n\nThe whole thing renders in about forty seconds. Change one line in the file, and you get a new video.\n\nOne system. Unlimited videos. And you never have to be on camera.\n\nFollow, I'm building this in public and sharing every piece of it.",
